== 4 types of ai
1. Reactive Machines
These AI systems act purely on the present situation. They cannot form memories or learn from past experiences, meaning they will always respond to identical situations in the same way. 

2. Limited Memory AI
This type of AI can look into the past to inform its future decisions. It uses pre-programmed data or data collected from recent interactions to make more informed predictions and responses. 


3. Theory of Mind AI
This is a conceptual type of AI that does not yet exist. It would be able to understand human thoughts, emotions, intentions, and beliefs, and be capable of forming opinions and social behaviors. 


4. Self-Aware AI
The ultimate future stage of AI. This theoretical AI would be capable of having its own consciousness, emotions, and needs, and would possess a true understanding of itself and its place in the world. 


== model ai governance framework
1. Decisions by AI should be explainable, transparent and fair
2. AI systems should be human centric

