= special pdpa

definitions
- individual: 1 person 
- organisation: group of >= 1 person(s)

- personal data: data that can identify an individual 
  - from the data
  - from the data and other info an organisation may have
- data intermediary: org which processes personal data on behalf of another org
- business contact info (BCI):
  - Name
  - Position or title
  - Business telephone number
  - Business address
  - Business electronic mail (email) address
  - Business fax number

PDPA covers data protection and do not call provisions.

== data protection
1. collect, use and dispose
2. care of PD
3. individuals autonomy


=== obligations
- consent obligation (user must consent)
- purpose limitation obligation (only collect necessary data)
- notification obligation (notify user about how data is used)
- accuracy obligation (accurate info)
- protection obligation (secure data from unauthorized access )
- retention limitation obligation (retain data for as long as necessary)
- transfer limitation obligation (transfer out of singapore must comply with PDPA)
- access and correction obligation (allow users to request to correct their data)
- accountability obligation (appoint DPO)
- data breach notification obligation (alert user for cyber incidents)

